       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4000 mg per dose four times daily is 16,000 mg/day, which is five times the usual maximum for ibuprofen. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for outpatients and 2,400 mg/day in most inpatient protocols. A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity.\n\nIt may be a typo, since 400 mg four times daily is a common dose. Which of these did you mean?\n\n- **400 mg** by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Another dose you'd like to specify\n\nIf 4000 mg per dose is what you want, tell me and add a note on the indication. I'd still want to confirm it, because it's far outside the safe range."
